module v2.test.manual.forensics_6280_synth_consumer

import v2.test.manual.forensics_6280_synth_producer { forensics_6280_synth_produce }
import v2.test.manual.forensics_6280_synth_owner_a { Rejected, SynthOwnerAAlt }

data forensics_6280_synth_repro_note: String = "Minimal synthetic reproducer for the wall-gap named in forensics_6280_tokenize_reject_locus.dag: forensics_6280_synth_owner_a/b/c.dag each declare an unrelated type with a bare Rejected variant (mirroring dag/std/markup.dag's MarkupSerializeResult.Rejected vs src/v2/std/diagnostic.dag's Outcome.Rejected, now 3-wide instead of 2 to widen any tie-break); forensics_6280_synth_producer.dag imports a SIBLING variant from each owner file (SynthOwnerAAlt/B/C) but never imports Rejected itself, then constructs a bare Rejected record with a declared return type of SynthOwnerA -- mirroring 01_tokenize.dag's own gap (imports Accepted, not Rejected, yet constructs bare Rejected). forensics_6280_synth_consumer.dag is import-pinned to SynthOwnerA's Rejected (the deterministic, wall-protected side) and reports whether the value it receives still resolves as that owner. RESULT (this session, executed not asserted): 40/40 runs stable at true (20 runs at 2 candidate owners, 20 more after adding a 3rd) -- no flip reproduced in a corpus this small. This does not refute the wall-gap (01_tokenize.dag's own import list is unchanged and still verifiably missing the Rejected import; see forensics_6280_tokenize_reject_locus.dag) -- it means the specific per-process randomization the battery observed on the real corpus (43-61 loaded sources) did not manifest at 4-6 files, so either scale of the candidate/source pool or some other environment-coupled factor (not merely candidate count) gates when the fallback path's pick actually varies. Reported honestly rather than asserted: this synthetic receipt is NEGATIVE at this scale, not a positive reproduction."

data forensics_6280_synth_scale_note: String = "Follow-on scale test (this session, same day): first confirmed gunbc run resolves only the TRANSITIVE IMPORT CLOSURE from --entry, not the whole --source-root tree -- an unimported decoy file sitting alongside these fixtures never entered the loaded set at all (5 sources resolved with it absent from imports; 6 once actually imported), so a decoy must be import-reachable from the entry to affect anything. With that corrected, added 40 more decoy modules (forensics_6280_synth_decoy_01..40.dag, each an unrelated 2-variant type, none named Rejected) all imported into forensics_6280_synth_producer.dag, pushing the loaded set to 46 sources -- inside the ~45-60 range the real corpus battery ran in. Reran the witness 10x at 46 sources: stable at true, 10/10, still zero flips. Combined with the earlier 40/40 at 4-6 sources: 60/60 total runs across a source-count range spanning roughly 4 to 46, all stable, no flip observed at any point on this synthetic tree. Reported as-is: candidate-count and loaded-source-count alone, at least up to the real corpus's own scale, do not reproduce the variance here -- whatever discriminates the two verdicts on the real tree is not fully captured by this reproducer's shape yet (content-identity/bucket-boundary sensitivity per sunny-wren-799's confound finding remains untested by this file specifically)."

data forensics_6280_synth_generic_note: String = "Follow-on: checked the REAL 01_tokenize.dag Rejected sites (lex_walk/tokenize, lines ~497/514) directly -- both are plain if/else branches inside functions with a DECLARED return type Outcome of TokenStream, not inside an un-annotated lambda body, so the lambda-position theory does not match this call site's actual shape. Outcome of T IS generic though, so reshaped forensics_6280_synth_owner_a.dag's SynthOwnerA into a generic SynthOwnerA of T (mirroring Outcome of T exactly: a Rejected variant with field reason of type String, and a SynthOwnerAAlt variant with field value of type T) and reran 10x at 46 loaded sources with the same generic-instantiation shape as the real Outcome of TokenStream. Still stable at true, 10/10, no flip. Separately found a second STATIC wall-hole matching sunny-wren-799's Terminal prediction: src/v2/extdeps/languages/ptx.dag imports a long list of names from v2.std.grammar (line 3-4) that does NOT include Terminal, yet constructs a bare Terminal record with fields token_class and stamp at line 128 (ptx_grammar_terminal) -- and dag/std/disposition.dag independently declares an unrelated Terminal variant with field reason of type NonEmptyStr. Same shape as 01_tokenize.dag's Rejected gap, unconfirmed whether it actually flips at runtime (declared return type GrammarExpr on that function, same shape as the stable synthetic above) but a second concrete, verifiable instance of the identical missing-import pattern, independent of Rejected."

fn forensics_6280_synth_witness_stable_owner() -> Bool {
  match forensics_6280_synth_produce() {
    Rejected { reason: _ } => true
    SynthOwnerAAlt { value: _ } => false
  }
}
